snp5.5:7.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp5.5:7.3 starts: above, below,
snp5.5:7.4 starts: Dispelling any delight,
snp5.5:7.5 starts: consciousness should not take a stance
snp5.5:10.1 starts: And they, too, would abandon stress
snp5.5:10.2 starts: those whom you, sage,
snp5.5:10.3 starts: Having met you, I bow down to you,
snp5.5:10.4 starts: Perhaps you will admonish me
snp5.6:4.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp5.6:4.2 starts: can I release from perplexity.
snp5.6:4.3 starts: But knowing the most excellent Dhamma,
snp5.6:4.4 starts: you will cross over this flood.
snp5.6:8.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp5.6:8.3 starts: above, below,
snp5.6:8.4 starts: Knowing it as a bond in the world,
snp5.6:8.5 starts: don’t create craving
snp5.8:2.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp5.8:2.2 starts: do the skilled here, Nanda,
snp5.8:2.3 starts: Those who live
snp5.8:2.4 starts: undesiring,
snp5.11:1.1 starts: For one stranded in the middle of the
snp5.11:1.3 starts: in the flood of great danger—birth—
snp5.11:1.4 starts: overwhelmed with aging & death:
snp5.11:1.5 starts: Tell me the island, dear sir,
snp5.11:1.6 starts: and show me the island
snp5.11:1.7 starts: so that this may not happen again.
